WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
Come and listen to a story about a man named Jed.

00:05.000 --> 00:08.000
He pulled a mountain here, barely kept his family fed.

00:08.000 --> 00:11.000
Then one day he was shooting out some food,

00:11.000 --> 00:14.000
and up through the ground caught a bubbling green.

00:14.000 --> 00:19.000
All that is, black gold, Texas tea.

00:19.000 --> 00:22.000
Well the first thing you know, Jed's a millionaire.

00:22.000 --> 00:25.000
Ken folks said, Jed move away from there.

00:25.000 --> 00:27.000
Said California, the place you ought to be.

00:27.000 --> 00:30.000
So they loaded up the truck and they moved to Beverly.

00:30.000 --> 00:35.000
Hills that is, swimming pools, movie stars,

00:35.000 --> 00:57.000
the Beverly Hillbillies.

00:57.000 --> 01:10.000
Well now listen here, fellow, don't be such a pig.

01:10.000 --> 01:15.000
Sorry, Floki, I didn't mean it.

01:15.000 --> 01:19.000
You're getting to be a right big-hell tea-lick.

01:19.000 --> 01:22.000
Billy May, get these varmints out of here.

01:22.000 --> 01:27.000
Granny, they ain't varmints, they're small critters.

01:27.000 --> 01:30.000
I don't care if they're your cousins.

01:30.000 --> 01:33.000
Get them out of my kitchen before I make stew out of them.

01:33.000 --> 01:43.000
Jed, all these critters are crowding me out of my own kitchen.

01:43.000 --> 01:46.000
How soon are you going to have my root cellar made?

01:46.000 --> 01:48.000
Well it won't be long now, Granny.

01:48.000 --> 01:49.000
Late Crick got the most of it done.

01:49.000 --> 01:52.000
Jed throwing me is going in there square off the corner and putting in the framing.

01:52.000 --> 01:53.000
Well let's hurry it up.

01:53.000 --> 01:56.000
I need a place where I can get off to myself.

01:56.000 --> 01:57.000
Well Jed's rolling down in the hole now.

01:57.000 --> 02:04.000
Let's go see how he's doing.

02:04.000 --> 02:06.000
Uncle Dark down there.

02:06.000 --> 02:08.000
How's it going, Jed Throw?

02:08.000 --> 02:09.000
Hey Uncle Dad.

02:09.000 --> 02:10.000
Hey Uncle Dad.

02:10.000 --> 02:13.000
Uncle Dad, pull me up.

02:13.000 --> 02:15.000
Okay, boy.

02:15.000 --> 02:17.000
Hold these dandy deep ones, Granny.

02:17.000 --> 02:19.000
Ain't nothing going to bother you down there.

02:19.000 --> 02:21.000
That suits me just fine.

02:21.000 --> 02:26.000
Of course when the cyclone comes up, I'll let the rest of you join me in my cellar.

02:26.000 --> 02:27.000
Thank you.

02:27.000 --> 02:29.000
Just till it blows over.

02:29.000 --> 02:35.000
And I want everybody out.

02:35.000 --> 02:36.000
Oh, good Jed, Granny.

02:36.000 --> 02:38.000
What you got smeared all over you?

02:38.000 --> 02:40.000
This here is oil.

02:40.000 --> 02:41.000
What?

02:41.000 --> 02:42.000
You done hit oil again.

02:42.000 --> 02:46.000
Last one I picked pretty soon was bubbling up and spurting all over the place.

02:46.000 --> 02:50.000
Well, there goes my root cellar.

02:50.000 --> 02:53.000
Let's look on the bright side, Granny.

02:53.000 --> 02:55.000
I think we're in time to plug it up.

02:55.000 --> 02:56.000
Yeah, true.

02:56.000 --> 02:58.000
You have to shovel.

02:58.000 --> 02:59.000
Help me fill in this hole.

02:59.000 --> 03:01.000
Don't you want the oil?

03:01.000 --> 03:04.000
I need more oil, I cussed you needed more engines.

03:04.000 --> 03:16.000
Hurry up, let's go.

03:16.000 --> 03:17.000
Good morning, Chief.

03:17.000 --> 03:18.000
Morning.

03:18.000 --> 03:22.000
Can you think of any reason why Jed Flammett would be digging a large hole in his backyard?

03:22.000 --> 03:23.000
No.

03:23.000 --> 03:28.000
Not unless he's going to take his money out of your bank and betty it.

03:28.000 --> 03:31.000
Sorry Chief.

03:31.000 --> 03:33.000
We do not joke about such things.

03:33.000 --> 03:35.000
Now find out why the Clampett's are digging.

03:35.000 --> 03:36.000
Yes, that's it.

03:36.000 --> 03:37.000
Big smile.

03:37.000 --> 03:38.000
Hold it.

03:38.000 --> 03:39.000
What's going on in my office?

03:39.000 --> 03:40.000
There's that.

03:40.000 --> 03:44.000
Well, it seems some girl from the secretarial pool has been chosen to represent the bank

03:44.000 --> 03:47.000
in the contest for Queen of Beverly Hills.

03:47.000 --> 03:49.000
Oh, Jed.

03:49.000 --> 03:56.000
It seems to me that intellectual measurement should determine who will represent this bank.

03:56.000 --> 04:01.000
You've got something there.

04:01.000 --> 04:04.000
Of course, she's got something there too.

04:04.000 --> 04:06.000
Good morning, Mr. Driesdale.

04:06.000 --> 04:08.000
Did we have a picture of you with your bank's representative?

04:08.000 --> 04:11.000
Well, it seems only fitting and proper.

04:11.000 --> 04:13.000
Hi, right over here in front of the desk, pardon me.

04:13.000 --> 04:18.000
Chief, I thought you agreed with me that intellect was more important than cheesecake.

04:18.000 --> 04:21.000
Oh yes, we do want an intellectual look.

04:21.000 --> 04:23.000
You are a secretary, right?

04:23.000 --> 04:30.000
Oh yes, sir, Mr. Driesdale.

04:30.000 --> 04:36.000
That's better.

04:36.000 --> 04:39.000
Excuse me.

04:39.000 --> 04:43.000
And now let's have a nice big smile.

04:43.000 --> 04:44.000
Hold it.

04:44.000 --> 04:46.000
Thank you, Mr. Driesdale.

04:46.000 --> 04:49.000
I'm sure your representative will win the race for Queen.

04:49.000 --> 04:50.000
Oh, I hope so.

04:50.000 --> 04:52.000
After all, that's what I'm paying you for.

04:52.000 --> 04:57.000
Good morning, Mrs. Driesdale.

04:57.000 --> 04:58.000
Good morning.

04:58.000 --> 05:01.000
Where is my husband's secretary?

05:01.000 --> 05:02.000
She's in his office with him.

05:02.000 --> 05:10.000
Thank you.

05:10.000 --> 05:13.000
Do you really take shorthand?

05:13.000 --> 05:15.000
Well, not very fast.

05:15.000 --> 05:22.000
It's not too important.

05:22.000 --> 05:24.000
She is a secretary?

05:24.000 --> 05:27.000
Word of honor, this is, uh...

05:27.000 --> 05:28.000
What is your name?

05:28.000 --> 05:29.000
Candy Davis.

05:29.000 --> 05:30.000
Candy, yes.

05:30.000 --> 05:33.000
Well, this is, uh...

05:33.000 --> 05:37.000
My name is Madgrits.

05:37.000 --> 05:39.000
Mrs. Driesdale.

05:39.000 --> 05:41.000
I think that your employee is dressed properly.

05:41.000 --> 05:43.000
Yes, he's an employee dressed properly.

05:43.000 --> 05:50.000
Dressed properly, employee.

05:50.000 --> 05:54.000
Well now, Milburn, there is another explanation that I'd like.

05:54.000 --> 05:56.000
Yes, dear?

05:56.000 --> 06:01.000
Those hillbilly friends of yours are defacing that beautiful estate next to us.

06:01.000 --> 06:04.000
They are burrowing about like so many goldfers.

06:04.000 --> 06:06.000
I want to know why.

06:06.000 --> 06:09.000
Well, I did ask somebody to look into that.

06:09.000 --> 06:12.000
You.

06:12.000 --> 06:13.000
Chief, I forgot.

06:13.000 --> 06:14.000
You forgot?

06:14.000 --> 06:17.000
I'll look into it immediately.

06:17.000 --> 06:21.000
Really, Milburn, I've taken all I can from those plant bits.

06:21.000 --> 06:22.000
Well, I haven't.

06:22.000 --> 06:25.000
That oil money still keeps rolling in.

06:25.000 --> 06:26.000
Why is it that important?

06:26.000 --> 06:29.000
Who steals my purse steals trash.

06:29.000 --> 06:35.000
Shake hands with a dedicated trash collector.

06:35.000 --> 06:39.000
I'm terribly sorry, but Miss Commerce Bank forgot her burner.

06:39.000 --> 06:41.000
What is this beauty contest nonsense?

06:41.000 --> 06:46.000
Well, it's in connection with Beverly Hills' 50th birthday celebration, the semi-centennial.

06:46.000 --> 06:48.000
You see, Margaret, it is important.

06:48.000 --> 06:50.000
The spotlight of the world will be on our fair city.

06:50.000 --> 06:52.000
And what will the spotlight show?

06:52.000 --> 06:56.000
Four unkempt hillbillies digging holes in the ground.

06:56.000 --> 07:00.000
Who's going to look at them with a hundred girls like this parading around?

07:00.000 --> 07:02.000
I told you to wait in my office.

07:02.000 --> 07:04.000
Oh, yes, ma'am.

07:04.000 --> 07:10.000
I hope you're not going to overlook the intellectual approach to this contest.

07:10.000 --> 07:13.000
The girl who wins will reign as queen of Beverly Hills.

07:13.000 --> 07:18.000
And she wins a trip around the world.

07:18.000 --> 07:22.000
That's it. Winning this beauty contest could solve everything.

07:22.000 --> 07:26.000
Oh, Margaret, Jane couldn't win with a rented figure.

07:26.000 --> 07:28.000
Kelly May Clampett could win.

07:28.000 --> 07:32.000
And naturally, her family will want to go around the world with her.

07:32.000 --> 07:33.000
I don't like the idea.

07:33.000 --> 07:36.000
Oh, please, Milben, just during the semi-centennial.

07:36.000 --> 07:37.000
No, Margaret, I don't like it.

07:37.000 --> 07:41.000
Very well. Mother will arrive tomorrow for a six-month visit.

07:41.000 --> 07:49.000
I like it.

07:49.000 --> 07:51.000
Margaret, can I stomp down good enough?

07:51.000 --> 07:56.000
Yep. There's nothing to spoil good ground like that smelly old oil.

07:56.000 --> 07:58.000
It sure is hard to wash off.

07:58.000 --> 08:00.000
Let me look at you, boy.

08:00.000 --> 08:02.000
Does that oil give your lye soap a real fight, Granny?

08:02.000 --> 08:04.000
Yeah, that pesky, messy old stuff.

08:04.000 --> 08:08.000
Now, I'm going to look for another spot to dig my root cellar.

08:08.000 --> 08:13.000
Maybe this time we'll get lucky and come up with a dry hole.

08:13.000 --> 08:14.000
Look here, honey.

08:14.000 --> 08:17.000
I don't want nothing said about us striking oil.

08:17.000 --> 08:18.000
Why not, pal?

08:18.000 --> 08:20.000
Because somebody will just go to force some more money on us,

08:20.000 --> 08:22.000
and we've got more than I share now.

08:22.000 --> 08:24.000
Yes, pal. Come bring the shovel.

08:24.000 --> 08:27.000
Okay, Granny.

08:27.000 --> 08:28.000
I reckon this is stomp down good enough.

08:28.000 --> 08:29.000
Come on, let's go give him a hand.

08:29.000 --> 08:30.000
Yes, sir, pal.

08:30.000 --> 08:32.000
Come on, Skipper.

08:32.000 --> 08:43.000
Don't just stand here with your fingers stuck in the ground. Do like Ellie said.

08:43.000 --> 08:50.000
Looks like no matter what we do, we're going to have oil.

08:50.000 --> 09:00.000
I declare it some days you just don't pay to get out of bed.

09:00.000 --> 09:03.000
I'm going to have a root cellar 60 foot deep,

09:03.000 --> 09:07.000
where I can sit alone and rock and never hear a peep.

09:07.000 --> 09:12.000
And if Ellie brings her little bean, I'll throw them out the door.

09:12.000 --> 09:17.000
And Hamptons don't dig me down 60 feet more.

09:17.000 --> 09:21.000
La dee da dee da dee da dee da dee da dee da.

09:21.000 --> 09:25.000
La dee da dee da dee da dee da dee da dee da.

09:25.000 --> 09:26.000
La dee da dee da.

09:26.000 --> 09:27.000
What happened?

09:27.000 --> 09:29.000
I've done struck oil again.

09:29.000 --> 09:31.000
It's a regular plague.

09:31.000 --> 09:33.000
It's a black day, Jethro.

09:33.000 --> 09:34.000
Sure enough, it's for me.

09:34.000 --> 09:37.000
I need a root cellar in the worst way.

09:37.000 --> 09:40.000
I've got some goat cheese that should have been put underground a year ago.

09:40.000 --> 09:44.000
If it gets any riper, it's going to run us out of the house.

09:44.000 --> 09:47.000
Look who's come to see us, Granny.

09:47.000 --> 09:49.000
Jethro, what have you been doing?

09:49.000 --> 09:51.000
Digging a hole in the ground.

09:51.000 --> 09:54.000
Jethro, we ain't talking about them holes, remember?

09:54.000 --> 09:56.000
Oh, I am. I was just trying to tell Miss Jane that every time I-

09:56.000 --> 09:58.000
Go on outside and wash up.

09:58.000 --> 09:59.000
Thank you.

09:59.000 --> 10:01.000
They don't get to get some.

10:01.000 --> 10:03.000
Don't talk, Jethro.

10:03.000 --> 10:07.000
Mr. Clavitt, we shouldn't have secrets from one another.

10:07.000 --> 10:10.000
Now let's discuss those holes you're digging.

10:10.000 --> 10:12.000
We better head in, Mr. Dryer.

10:12.000 --> 10:14.000
They'll probably get you all stirred up.

10:14.000 --> 10:15.000
What?

10:15.000 --> 10:17.000
Is it about your money?

10:17.000 --> 10:18.000
Tell me.

10:18.000 --> 10:20.000
You see, you're stirred up already.

10:20.000 --> 10:23.000
Let me ask Mr. Clavitt's help with my problem.

10:23.000 --> 10:25.000
Perhaps that will solve yours.

10:25.000 --> 10:27.000
Could we step outside?

10:27.000 --> 10:29.000
Well, if there are not too fur outside.

10:29.000 --> 10:30.000
Very well.

10:30.000 --> 10:35.000
Why don't you stay and visit with Granny?

10:35.000 --> 10:45.000
Granny, let me tell you some of the advantages of the modern day bank vault over, say, a hole in the ground.

10:45.000 --> 10:51.000
Mr. Clavitt, the City of Beverly Hills is about to choose a queen.

10:51.000 --> 10:52.000
You don't say?

10:52.000 --> 10:53.000
Yes.

10:53.000 --> 10:55.000
A number of beautiful girls have entered the race.

10:55.000 --> 10:56.000
How many you got running?

10:56.000 --> 11:00.000
Quite a few, but there's always room for one or two more.

11:00.000 --> 11:04.000
And another advantage is that our vault is nice and dry.

11:04.000 --> 11:06.000
In fact, air conditioned.

11:06.000 --> 11:10.000
Things become moldy and damp when left underground too long.

11:10.000 --> 11:12.000
Now I'd know that to happen.

11:12.000 --> 11:18.000
But it would be a mite unhandy for me to have to go clean down to your bank every time I wanted something.

11:18.000 --> 11:19.000
But you won't have to.

11:19.000 --> 11:24.000
You just pick up the phone, tell me how much you want and when you want it, and it'll be here like, pa!

11:24.000 --> 11:26.000
You know?

11:26.000 --> 11:27.000
Yes, ma'am.

11:27.000 --> 11:30.000
Now that'll be much handier than using your own backyard vault.

11:30.000 --> 11:31.000
Yeah.

11:31.000 --> 11:36.000
Especially after all the trouble we had trying to dig them holes out there.

11:36.000 --> 11:39.000
Now, here are some of the other advantages.

11:39.000 --> 11:45.000
And in addition to reigning over the City of Beverly Hills as queen, the winner will also get a trip around the world.

11:45.000 --> 11:47.000
Woo doggies.

11:47.000 --> 11:48.000
Yes.

11:48.000 --> 11:54.000
There'll be parties and dances, she'll be the center of attention, besieged by handsome, eligible men.

11:54.000 --> 11:59.000
You know something like this is exactly what Ellie Mae needs to turn her into a lady.

11:59.000 --> 12:00.000
You are right.

12:00.000 --> 12:02.000
What a wonderful idea.

12:02.000 --> 12:04.000
And she's got a chance of winning?

12:04.000 --> 12:10.000
Mr. Plattford, if Ellie Mae runs for queen, I can practically assure you that she will win the race.

12:10.000 --> 12:12.000
I hope I can get her to run.

12:12.000 --> 12:17.000
Ed, Mr. Guy Dale has done top me into not digging any more holes.

12:17.000 --> 12:20.000
I'm for keeping everything in the vault down to his back.

12:20.000 --> 12:22.000
What do you say, Granny?

12:22.000 --> 12:24.000
Come on in and help me talk something.

12:24.000 --> 12:28.000
I'll be right back.

12:28.000 --> 12:30.000
You know what, Granny?

12:30.000 --> 12:32.000
The City of Beverly Hills is going to have a queen.

12:32.000 --> 12:33.000
No.

12:33.000 --> 12:34.000
And you know how they're going to pick the queen?

12:34.000 --> 12:35.000
How?

12:35.000 --> 12:38.000
They're going to have all the girls run for the race.

12:38.000 --> 12:40.000
I'll be sweet.

12:40.000 --> 12:42.000
Congratulations, Steve.

12:42.000 --> 12:43.000
You did a great job.

12:43.000 --> 12:45.000
I was mildly magnificent.

12:45.000 --> 12:46.000
How did you do?

12:46.000 --> 12:47.000
Mission accomplished.

12:47.000 --> 12:53.000
Ellie Mae will enter the race for queen and the finals will be held beside the club at swimming pool.

12:53.000 --> 12:54.000
Bye, George.

12:54.000 --> 12:55.000
Not calling for a raise.

12:55.000 --> 12:56.000
Oh, Jesus.

12:56.000 --> 12:57.000
So long, I do feel.

12:57.000 --> 12:58.000
Oh, no, it isn't.

12:58.000 --> 13:06.000
I deserve a raise and I'm going to have it.

13:06.000 --> 13:07.000
Hey, Alice Drydale.

13:07.000 --> 13:12.000
Granny tells me you don't keep all these little fur down in the vault in your bank.

13:12.000 --> 13:13.000
I said, oh, Jim.

13:13.000 --> 13:17.000
If ever I need anything, he's going to fetch it out here himself.

13:17.000 --> 13:19.000
Yeah, that is surpassing kind.

13:19.000 --> 13:23.000
I wouldn't open that until you get it down to that air conditioned vault.

13:23.000 --> 13:24.000
Granny's got cheese in there.

13:24.000 --> 13:28.000
It'll walk down to the bank by itself and give it a chance.

13:28.000 --> 13:29.000
Look up, Chief.

13:29.000 --> 13:31.000
Half of victory is better than none.

13:31.000 --> 13:35.000
When you hear who's going to run in the race for queen of Beverly Hills.

13:35.000 --> 13:36.000
I heard.

13:36.000 --> 13:38.000
And I think Ellie Mae will win.

13:38.000 --> 13:42.000
Don't be too sure.

13:42.000 --> 13:43.000
Who could possibly beat her?

13:43.000 --> 13:44.000
Granny's going to try.

13:44.000 --> 13:45.000
What?

13:45.000 --> 13:46.000
Granny, you haven't got a chance.

13:46.000 --> 13:47.000
We'll see about that.

13:47.000 --> 13:48.000
My legs have ever been as good as Ellie Mae's.

13:48.000 --> 13:49.000
Well, don't just stand there.

13:49.000 --> 13:50.000
Pick up your basket and let's get back to the vault.

13:50.000 --> 13:51.000
Where do they come off thinking I ain't got a chance to be queen?

13:51.000 --> 13:52.000
Now, cool down, Granny.

13:52.000 --> 13:53.000
I reckon they just never seen how fast you can run.

13:53.000 --> 13:54.000
Oh, I'm sorry.

13:54.000 --> 13:55.000
I'm sorry.

13:55.000 --> 13:56.000
I'm sorry.

13:56.000 --> 13:57.000
I'm sorry.

13:57.000 --> 13:58.000
I'm sorry.

13:58.000 --> 13:59.000
I'm sorry.

13:59.000 --> 14:00.000
I'm sorry.

14:00.000 --> 14:01.000
I'm sorry.

14:01.000 --> 14:02.000
I'm sorry.

14:02.000 --> 14:03.000
I'm sorry.

14:03.000 --> 14:04.000
I'm sorry.

14:04.000 --> 14:05.000
I'm sorry.

14:05.000 --> 14:06.000
I'm sorry.

14:06.000 --> 14:07.000
I'm sorry.

14:07.000 --> 14:08.000
I'm sorry.

14:08.000 --> 14:09.000
I'm sorry.

14:09.000 --> 14:16.080
I'm sorry Granny, I reckon they just never seen how fast you can run.

14:16.080 --> 14:21.180
Granny, you and Ellie ready to run?

14:21.180 --> 14:22.180
Yeah, Dad.

14:22.180 --> 14:28.220
I'll start you quick as I get this pistol loaded.

14:28.220 --> 14:32.200
Okay, now Ellie, I want you to run your best way to get me.

14:32.200 --> 14:33.360
It'll be good practice for us.

14:33.360 --> 14:35.820
How can I have the practice, Granny?

14:35.820 --> 14:37.860
You know we can beat these city women.

14:37.860 --> 14:41.860
Yeah, but this is gonna be a waning of a race betwixt you and me.

14:41.860 --> 14:44.860
And I ain't done no top speed running lately.

14:44.860 --> 14:47.860
Granny, you don't have to be made a big queen of Beverly Hills.

14:47.860 --> 14:49.860
I don't care shots about it.

14:49.860 --> 14:51.860
No, Ellie, your pa wants you in the race.

14:51.860 --> 14:54.860
And I gotta beat you fair and square.

14:54.860 --> 14:56.860
On your mark.

14:56.860 --> 14:58.860
Now do your best to get me.

14:58.860 --> 15:11.860
Get set.

15:11.860 --> 15:12.860
Good one, Jed.

15:12.860 --> 15:14.860
Well, you fasted me.

15:14.860 --> 15:16.860
Feels like Ellie was out in front of you a little.

15:16.860 --> 15:17.860
That don't mean nothing.

15:17.860 --> 15:21.860
She's out in front of me standing still.

15:21.860 --> 15:28.860
Maybe you better sit down for a spell.

15:28.860 --> 15:32.860
Granny, you sure you want to race against all them young girls?

15:32.860 --> 15:34.860
You're darn tootin'.

15:34.860 --> 15:37.860
I'd do anything to be queen of Beverly Hills.

15:37.860 --> 15:38.860
How come you're so anxious?

15:38.860 --> 15:42.860
Cause when I'm queen, folks will have to do what I tell them to.

15:42.860 --> 15:46.860
And I got a lot of changes in mind for this town.

15:46.860 --> 15:48.860
Sorry I beat you, Granny.

15:48.860 --> 15:53.860
You only beat me because we was running on level city pavement.

15:53.860 --> 15:55.860
I'm a stump jumper and a hedge hopper.

15:55.860 --> 15:56.860
You did.

15:56.860 --> 15:59.860
You and Jeff will wrestle me up something to jump over.

15:59.860 --> 16:02.860
I'll show this youngin' how to run.

16:02.860 --> 16:06.860
Well, Granny, you might could get hurt.

16:06.860 --> 16:10.860
Like I said, Granny, I don't care nothing about being queen.

16:10.860 --> 16:12.860
You don't have to race me.

16:12.860 --> 16:14.860
Now you listen to me.

16:14.860 --> 16:18.860
Both of ya, if I'm gonna sit on the throne of Beverly Hills,

16:18.860 --> 16:21.860
these legs is gonna take me there.

16:21.860 --> 16:23.860
You get ready to run.

16:23.860 --> 16:26.860
And don't hold back.

16:26.860 --> 16:29.860
On your mark.

16:29.860 --> 16:50.860
Get set.

16:50.860 --> 16:52.860
How'd we do that time, Jim?

16:52.860 --> 16:54.860
I'm afraid the youngin' made you again.

16:54.860 --> 16:55.860
You ready to sit down and rest now?

16:55.860 --> 17:07.860
No, I'm just coming to get membered out.

17:07.860 --> 17:08.860
Hello?

17:08.860 --> 17:09.860
Don?

17:09.860 --> 17:11.860
Well, I don't care what it smells like.

17:11.860 --> 17:16.860
It stays in the vault until I say take it out.

17:16.860 --> 17:18.860
I've got some great news, Mr. Drysdale.

17:18.860 --> 17:19.860
What is it?

17:19.860 --> 17:22.860
Come in, Candy.

17:22.860 --> 17:24.860
We have just come from the first press party.

17:24.860 --> 17:27.860
And I went around and spoke to every judge personally.

17:27.860 --> 17:29.860
This young lady was the unanimous favorite.

17:29.860 --> 17:31.860
A sure winner.

17:31.860 --> 17:32.860
Kidding.

17:32.860 --> 17:33.860
With a lot of your money, Mr. Drysdale,

17:33.860 --> 17:35.860
the blinding and dining those fellas sure paid off.

17:35.860 --> 17:39.860
Tomorrow this girl will be the queen of Beverly Hills.

17:39.860 --> 17:41.860
Mr. Chief, if you would use the intellectual approach,

17:41.860 --> 17:44.860
as I urged, we would not be in this mess.

17:44.860 --> 17:45.860
What do you mean, we?

17:45.860 --> 17:47.860
This is your problem, remember?

17:47.860 --> 17:49.860
If you'll excuse us, we'd like to go downstairs.

17:49.860 --> 17:50.860
I got a great idea for a picture.

17:50.860 --> 17:54.860
Yes, he's going to photograph me inside the vault.

17:54.860 --> 17:57.860
No, let them go.

17:57.860 --> 18:02.860
This might eliminate her right there.

18:02.860 --> 18:05.860
Granny, you've got to slow down, Drysdale.

18:05.860 --> 18:07.860
Where do you get off like that,

18:07.860 --> 18:09.860
giving orders to the next queen of Beverly Hills?

18:09.860 --> 18:12.860
No, queen, you've been running for two hours straight.

18:12.860 --> 18:14.860
And as soon as Ellie May gets her wind,

18:14.860 --> 18:17.860
I'm going to race her to Pasadena and back.

18:17.860 --> 18:19.860
Come in.

18:19.860 --> 18:24.860
Oh, Granny, I'm struck to you immediately about running for queen.

18:24.860 --> 18:26.860
You in the race, Ellie?

18:26.860 --> 18:29.860
Oh, no, I'm hardly at my best in a bathing suit.

18:29.860 --> 18:32.860
Bathing suit? Why would you wear one of them things?

18:32.860 --> 18:34.860
Well, all contestants have to wear bathing suits.

18:34.860 --> 18:35.860
Not me.

18:35.860 --> 18:36.860
But it's one of the rules.

18:36.860 --> 18:38.860
Then I'm taking myself out of the race.

18:38.860 --> 18:39.860
I don't blame you, Granny.

18:39.860 --> 18:43.860
Why, if I was to show up in one of them skimpy bathing suits,

18:43.860 --> 18:46.860
it might start the men folks to fighting over me.

18:46.860 --> 18:49.860
I hear tell that these city men are bolder to begin with.

18:49.860 --> 18:52.860
One of them rascals might run up and laugh at me

18:52.860 --> 18:56.860
and hug me and kiss me and help me off and marry me.

18:56.860 --> 19:00.860
And I just put myself back in the race.

19:00.860 --> 19:03.860
So, you see, Miss Davis, being a beauty queen isn't all fun.

19:03.860 --> 19:05.860
It's lots of hard work, too.

19:05.860 --> 19:07.860
Oh, I won't mind that.

19:07.860 --> 19:11.860
I'll just keep thinking about that wonderful trip around the world.

19:11.860 --> 19:14.860
Wonderful.

19:14.860 --> 19:17.860
Have you ever had those shots they give you?

19:17.860 --> 19:19.860
It's a nightmare.

19:19.860 --> 19:21.860
Your arms will ache for weeks

19:21.860 --> 19:23.860
and you'll break out these large black and blue bumps

19:23.860 --> 19:27.860
and sometimes break out in a rash.

19:27.860 --> 19:29.860
Well, other people have gone through it.

19:29.860 --> 19:31.860
I guess I can.

19:31.860 --> 19:33.860
Now wait, you haven't heard the worst part.

19:33.860 --> 19:34.860
That's right, Steve.

19:34.860 --> 19:36.860
I'm representing your bank.

19:36.860 --> 19:37.860
Don't you want me to win?

19:37.860 --> 19:39.860
Of course I do.

19:39.860 --> 19:41.860
But I feel responsible.

19:41.860 --> 19:44.860
I feel duty bound to show you both sides of the picture.

19:44.860 --> 19:46.860
You might want to drop out.

19:46.860 --> 19:49.860
Now, don't you worry about that.

19:49.860 --> 19:51.860
Nothing can discourage me.

19:51.860 --> 19:53.860
I'm going to win that contest for you.

19:53.860 --> 19:55.860
Thanks a million.

19:55.860 --> 20:00.860
Well, Chief, mission accomplished.

20:00.860 --> 20:03.860
Ellie May will be the sole and frisbee of the Clarket family.

20:03.860 --> 20:05.860
How did you do?

20:05.860 --> 20:06.860
No good.

20:06.860 --> 20:07.860
Shut up.

20:07.860 --> 20:10.860
Ellie has a good chance of beating her.

20:10.860 --> 20:13.860
Oh, Miss Hathaway, Mr. Drysdale,

20:13.860 --> 20:15.860
can we be getting back to town?

20:15.860 --> 20:18.860
I have a date tonight with the head judge.

20:18.860 --> 20:26.860
Ladies and gentlemen,

20:26.860 --> 20:32.860
we have reached a decision.

20:32.860 --> 20:35.860
The finalists are

20:35.860 --> 20:37.860
the representative of the Commerce Bank,

20:37.860 --> 20:38.860
Miss Cady Davis,

20:38.860 --> 20:41.860
and our unsponsored contestant,

20:41.860 --> 20:57.860
Miss Ellie May Plampett.

20:57.860 --> 21:01.860
Excuse me, Mr. Milburn Drysdale,

21:01.860 --> 21:02.860
the president of the Commerce Bank,

21:02.860 --> 21:03.860
has an announcement to make.

21:03.860 --> 21:05.860
Thank you, Mr. Cummings.

21:05.860 --> 21:10.860
Due to circumstances beyond her control,

21:10.860 --> 21:13.860
Miss Cady Davis has been forced to withdraw from the contest.

21:13.860 --> 21:16.860
However, ladies and gentlemen,

21:16.860 --> 21:18.860
she will receive a trip around the world

21:18.860 --> 21:21.860
at the expense of the bank.

21:21.860 --> 21:24.860
And a substitute will appear in her place.

21:24.860 --> 21:27.860
Our two finalists will please come forward.

21:27.860 --> 21:42.860
Miss Clappett first.

21:42.860 --> 21:59.860
And now the new entry representing the Commerce Bank.

21:59.860 --> 22:01.860
Are you kidding?

22:01.860 --> 22:02.860
No.

22:02.860 --> 22:05.860
The Commerce Bank feels intellectual measurements

22:05.860 --> 22:07.860
are more important than physical ones,

22:07.860 --> 22:10.860
and we have every confidence that you will agree with us.

22:10.860 --> 22:13.860
Are you kidding?

22:13.860 --> 22:16.860
Each contestant will now step to the microphone

22:16.860 --> 22:18.860
and tell us in her own words

22:18.860 --> 22:21.860
how she intends to represent the city of Beverly Hills

22:21.860 --> 22:24.860
as queen on her world tour.

22:24.860 --> 22:26.860
Miss Jane Hathaway.

22:26.860 --> 22:28.860
Ladies and gentlemen,

22:28.860 --> 22:31.860
if I am so fortunate as to win,

22:31.860 --> 22:34.860
can I rest assure that I will carry the message

22:34.860 --> 22:37.860
of our cultural and intellectual achievements

22:37.860 --> 22:40.860
to our sister cities from...

22:40.860 --> 22:45.860
from Pone to Pone.

22:45.860 --> 22:50.860
And now we will hear from the winner.

22:50.860 --> 22:54.860
I mean, Miss Clappett.

22:54.860 --> 22:57.860
Well, first off, I'm going to take my critters,

22:57.860 --> 22:59.860
especially my skunk, along with me.

22:59.860 --> 23:01.860
Because critters, especially skunks,

23:01.860 --> 23:05.860
don't get much of a chance to try out.

23:05.860 --> 23:08.860
I'm going to take my pal and granny and Jeffro

23:08.860 --> 23:11.860
and our hound dog, old Duke, with me.

23:11.860 --> 23:15.860
I'll be mighty proud to represent the city of Beverly Hills.

23:15.860 --> 23:17.860
But it's just between you and me,

23:17.860 --> 23:21.860
I'd hate rather Miss Jane here would win.

23:21.860 --> 23:26.860
One moment, please.

23:26.860 --> 23:28.860
Find the right elevator, right good speech, Indji.

23:28.860 --> 23:29.860
First right.

23:29.860 --> 23:35.860
Donners, how proud.

23:35.860 --> 23:38.860
Ladies and gentlemen,

23:38.860 --> 23:40.860
may I have your attention, please?

23:40.860 --> 23:43.860
Quiet, please.

23:43.860 --> 23:45.860
After due deliberation,

23:45.860 --> 23:49.860
our judges have come to a unanimous decision.

23:49.860 --> 23:51.860
The young lady who will represent

23:51.860 --> 23:53.860
the city of Beverly Hills as queen

23:53.860 --> 23:58.860
is none other than our distinguished judge,

23:58.860 --> 24:11.860
Miss Karen Cranston.

24:11.860 --> 24:12.860
I'm so grateful to Bob.

24:12.860 --> 24:13.860
I mean, Mr. Cummings.

24:13.860 --> 24:24.860
I mean, the head judge.

24:24.860 --> 24:25.860
Where are you going, granny?

24:25.860 --> 24:28.860
I'm going to throw her in the cement pond,

24:28.860 --> 24:31.860
her and them other goomer judges with you.

24:31.860 --> 24:56.860
I don't have any money.

24:56.860 --> 25:24.860
I'm getting all this kid.

25:24.860 --> 25:27.860
Listen to the story about a man named Jed.

25:27.860 --> 25:32.860
Then one day he was eating at some food

25:32.860 --> 25:35.860
and he met a foodie ground called the Brooklyn Groove.

25:35.860 --> 25:40.860
All that is black gold, Texas tea.

25:40.860 --> 25:42.860
Well, the first thing you know,

25:42.860 --> 26:02.860
Jed's a millionaire.

